NOT LEGAL ADVICE
----------------
qa-gate automates checks for the presence, technical behaviour and dates of legal requirements that apply to
websites and software in Germany and the EU (DSGVO, TTDSG, DDG, BFSG, KI-VO/AI Act, PAngV, VSBG and the
profession-specific rules in the sector packs). It does not assess the legal quality of texts, it cannot know the
facts of a concrete business, and laws, court decisions and authority guidance change. Every rule carries the
source it was derived from and every sector pack lists the open questions ("pruefen") a lawyer must settle.
Before relying on a result for a real deployment, a client contract or a regulated profession, consult a lawyer
specialised in German IT, competition and data-protection law. The AI features of qa-gate (configuration
suggestions, legal-rule drafts, triage) are proposals for a human to review; they never produce a verdict.

